WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500 align:center
The Cost of Complexity asks what it costs
to distinguish more outcomes.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000 align:center
The manuscript, its files and the editing
conversation share one workspace.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.500 align:center
On 18 November, one proposal covered
more than 50 edits across eight TeX files.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.000 align:center
The app keeps the original proposal
and links to the later revision.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.667 align:center
This staged excerpt revisits a claim
about the cost of subdividing a square.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:30.958 align:center
The author edits the proposed sentence.
The new wording prices each split by area.

00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:38.000 align:center
Accept saves the author’s wording
to the excerpt. Undo is available.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000 align:center
A separate check splits a square
into 256 cells over four rounds.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000 align:center
The run records 85 splits. Total cost is
4 by area and 15 by wall length.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.500 align:center
The plot reads each round’s totals
from the CSV and links back to the run.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.000 align:center
The app rebuilds the manuscript
with the new plot and its caption.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000 align:center
This example workflow routes the draft
to an independent evidence reviewer.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000 align:center
The app rechecks an 11-file arXiv package
from the saved 18 November manuscript.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000 align:center
Both LaTeX passes succeed.
The text matches across all 21 pages.
